{
  "title": "Vendor Portal FAQ",
  "source": "vendor-portal/faq",
  "url": "https://help.medipyxis.com/vendor-portal/faq/",
  "commit": "5d93bb5 (live on main)",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "vpf-01",
      "claim": "Answers to the questions vendor staff ask most often about the vendor portal (/vendor).",
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "path: \"/vendor\",",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/router.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "element: <VendorShell />,",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/router.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vpf-02",
      "claim": "Can I see patient-level data? No. The portal does not expose PHI. Where a patient is referenced — for example on the Use Events page — you see only minimal, de-identified detail such as the patient's initials and year of birth, never a name, full date of birth, or diagnosis.",
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "{evt.patient_display.initials}",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorUseEventsPage.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "// PHI-safe: view exposes patient_initials + birth_year only.",
          "paths": [
            "backend/supabase/functions/vendor-list-use-events/index.ts"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "{line.patient_initials} {line.patient_birth_year}",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorInvoiceDetailPage.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        }
      ],
      "reason": "The display is limited to initials and year of birth (checked). Note: initials plus year of birth are limited data, not HIPAA de-identified; 'does not expose PHI' is a legal characterization this runner cannot confirm."
    },
    {
      "id": "vpf-03",
      "claim": "What are the two vendor roles? vendor_admin — full access, including the Staff page to invite and manage colleagues. vendor_user — everything except Staff (Orders, Use Events, Catalog, Invoices, Clinics).",
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "vendor_sales",
          "paths": [
            "backend/supabase/functions/_shared/vendor-auth.ts"
          ],
          "expect": "absent"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "note": "vendor_user would see every page except Staff",
          "pattern": "<Route path=\"/settings/api\" element={<VendorAdminOnly><VendorSettingsApiPage /></VendorAdminOnly>} />",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorRoutes.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "absent"
        }
      ],
      "finding": "There are three roles: vendor_admin (Admin), vendor_user (Staff) and vendor_sales (Sales) (VendorShell.tsx). Besides Staff, the API page and editing clinic terms are admin-only (VendorRoutes.tsx, vendor-terms-upsert).",
      "proposed_text": "What are the vendor roles? Admin (vendor_admin) — every page, plus Staff (invite and manage colleagues), API (API keys and webhooks), and editing each clinic's terms. Staff (vendor_user) and Sales (vendor_sales) — every page except Staff, API, and clinic terms. The Staff page invites people as Admin or Staff.",
      "proposed_checks": [
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "vendor_admin: \"Admin\",",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/components/app-shell/VendorShell.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "vendor_user: \"Staff\",",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/components/app-shell/VendorShell.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "vendor_sales: \"Sales\",",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/components/app-shell/VendorShell.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "<Route path=\"/staff\" element={<VendorAdminOnly><VendorStaffPage /></VendorAdminOnly>} />",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorRoutes.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "<Route path=\"/settings/api\" element={<VendorAdminOnly><VendorSettingsApiPage /></VendorAdminOnly>} />",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorRoutes.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "<Route path=\"/clinics/:id/terms\" element={<VendorAdminOnly><VendorTermsPage /></VendorAdminOnly>} />",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorRoutes.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "description: \"API keys and webhooks\"",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/components/app-shell/VendorShell.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "if (ident.identity.role !== \"vendor_admin\") {",
          "paths": [
            "backend/supabase/functions/vendor-terms-upsert/index.ts"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "if (identity?.role === \"vendor_admin\") {",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/components/app-shell/VendorShell.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "items.push(...VENDOR_ADMIN_NAV_ITEMS);",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/components/app-shell/VendorShell.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "<option value=\"vendor_user\">vendor_user</option>",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorStaffPage.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "<option value=\"vendor_admin\">vendor_admin</option>",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorStaffPage.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "<option value=\"vendor_sales\"",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorStaffPage.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "absent"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vpf-04",
      "claim": "How do orders reach me? Clinics place orders that appear on your Orders page as Pending. You accept them (In Progress), ship with a tracking number (Shipped), and they complete as Delivered.",
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "status: \"pending\", // T3",
          "paths": [
            "backend/supabase/functions/create-vendor-order/index.ts"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": ".from(\"vendor_orders\")",
          "paths": [
            "backend/supabase/functions/create-vendor-order/index.ts"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "Mark Delivered",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorOrderDetailDrawer.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "placeholder=\"Tracking #\"",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorOrderDetailDrawer.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "{ key: 'progress',  label: 'In Progress',  statuses: ['accepted', 'in_progress'] },",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorOrdersPage.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vpf-05",
      "kind": "advice",
      "claim": "There is no UIN/receiving step on the vendor side.",
      "reason": "A statement of absence about vendor workflow; receiving is clinic-side (verified in live-vendor-portal-receiving.json)."
    },
    {
      "id": "vpf-06",
      "claim": "How do I add or change a product? Manage your SKUs on the Catalog page — click New SKU or edit an existing one.",
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "New SKU",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorCatalogPage.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        }
      ],
      "finding": "The button is 'Add Product'; there is no 'New SKU' button (VendorCatalogPage.tsx at v1.1.345).",
      "proposed_text": "On the Catalog page, click Add Product, or click a row to edit it.",
      "proposed_checks": [
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "Add Product",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorCatalogPage.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        },
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "onClick={() => openEdit(item)}",
          "paths": [
            "frontend/src/pages/vendor/VendorCatalogPage.tsx"
          ],
          "expect": "present"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vpf-07",
      "claim": "Changes take effect directly; there is no separate practice approval step.",
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "grep",
          "fixed": true,
          "pattern": "status: \"proposed\",",
          "paths": [
            "backend/supabase/functions/vendor-catalog-push/index.ts"
